### Page 3 of 32

```text
Page 1 of 8
CONTRACT NO.__________

DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT
BETWEEN THE CITY OF CHEYENNE AND
LARAMIE COUNTY SCHOOL DISTRICT NUMBER ONE

1.
Parties.  This DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT (the "Agreement") is made and entered
into by and between Laramie County School District Number One (District), whose address is
2810 House Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001, and the City of Cheyenne, a municipality
organized and existing under the laws of the State of Wyoming (City), whose address is 2101
O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.

2.
Purpose.

WHEREAS the District is developing the Coyote Ridge Elementary School project on the
east side of Powderhouse Road between Dell Range Boulevard and Storey Boulevard, southeast
of the intersection of Powderhouse Road and Carlson Street, as outlined on the map attached hereto
as Exhibit A, and;

WHEREAS, the Development will result in impacts to the City’s infrastructure system,
and;
WHEREAS, the purpose of this AGREEMENT is to outline responsibilities of the City
and the District for public infrastructure improvements relating to the Development, and;

WHEREAS, the District understands this development requires construction of offsite
improvements to serve the Development including the extension of Carlson Street eastward from
Powderhouse Road, as indicated on Exhibit A; said extension includes curb and gutter and other
typical development requirements of the City, and;

WHERAS, both parties understand the mutual benefit associated with the construction of
Coyote Ridge Elementary to the community and children served by both the District and City, and;

WHEREAS, at the same time Monument Home Builders, Inc. is developing the Harmony
Valley, First Filing subdivision which is located south of South High School, between South High
School and West College Drive, as indicated on the map attached hereto as Exhibit B, and:

WHEREAS, the City has agreed as part of said development to participate in the future
extension of Cribbon Avenue, which is on the west side of the South High School property, south
into Harmony Valley First Filing, also indicated on Exhibit B, and;

WHEREAS, in order to extend Cribbon Avenue as outlined above, the City must acquire
a 3.3-acre parcel of land owned by the District situated on the southwest portion of the South High
School property, as indicated in Exhibit B, now therefore;
By Stefanie Boster at 11:04 am, Mar 09, 2022
```

### Page 4 of 32

```text
Page 2 of 8

WHEREAS, the District has asked for the City to participate in construction costs
associated with Carlson Street within the Coyote Ridge Subdivision, and;

WHEREAS, the District has provided appraisals demonstrating that lands shown in Exhibit
B plus the estimated District proposed Carlson Street right-of-way improvements are in order of
magnitude equal to the estimated monetary value of the total Carlson Street right-of-way
improvements required by the City of Cheyenne municipal code that will be constructed at a later
date.

WHEREAS, the District and City agree that the West ingress/egress access point on
Powderhouse Road shall be perpetual and permanent in nature and remain as illustrated on the
approved construction documents.  However, the City reserves its right to change the access to a
“right in/out” only upon the City’s demonstration that operational efficiencies or safety are being
impaired, specifically due to the southbound to eastbound left turn from Powderhouse Road.

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the promises of the parties hereto and other good
and valuable consideration, the receipt and adequacy of which are hereby acknowledged, the
Parties agree as follows:

3.
Terms of Agreement.

A.
Recitals Incorporated.  The foregoing recitals are incorporated herein by reference
into this AGREEMENT as though set forth at length and shall be separate design plans
from the internal civil improvements.

B.
Both parties understand that the municipal code requires the District to construct,
at its cost, all public and private improvements (development improvements) necessitated
by the development itself and required to mitigate offsite impacts associated with the
development in accordance with Chapter 1.16 Annexation and Infrastructure
Improvements of the Cheyenne Municipal Code.

C.
The City understands that the State Construction Department budget provided to
District did not contain funding to fully program for the offsite financial requirements
associated with the infrastructure improvements of Carlson Street.

D.
In exchange for the delivery of said 3.3-acre parcel to the fee possession of the City
by the District, the City will relieve the District of certain offsite roadway public
improvements for Carlson Street in accordance with Exhibit A and this agreement.

E.
In agreeing to the exchange, the City has considered the benefit of the additional
right-of-way for curb and gutter and offsite improvements granted by the District to the
City along the east side of Powderhouse Road, (typically double the 10’ width of said right-
of-way), as indicated on Exhibit A.
