```text
Page 3 of 8
F.
The value of the District’s 3.3-acre parcel and said additional rights-of-way equals
$265,000 (Exhibit B). The estimated total construction cost of the District proposed
Carlson Street improvements in entirety has been estimated in 2021 at $705,000 (Exhibit
C.2).   The estimated total participatory construction costs for Carlson Street are anticipated
to be $590,000 for the District and $118,000 for the City including item G below (See
Exhibit C.2). The final value of the improvements will be based on the lowest, qualified,
responsive bid accepted by the District.

G.
The City agrees to compensate the District for the additional 2-foot width of
concrete sidewalk and crushed base requested oversizing of offsite public concrete
sidewalk improvements adjacent to Carlson Street and Powderhouse Road which are
associated with this development.   The estimated total construction costs for those
improvements are included in Item F and Exhibit C.2.

4.
Commencement Date.  This AGREEMENT shall commence on the date when fully
executed by all parties.

5.
Payment.  Upon receiving itemized invoices from the District, the City agrees to pay the
District for a portion of the accepted and approved Carlson Street improvements and associated
oversizing of adjacent public sidewalk as illustrated in Exhibit A and C.2. Such costs shall include,
but not necessarily be limited to, materials, labor, and incidentals required to construct the Carlson
Street improvements, as determined by the successful bidder in the amount as outlined in Section
3, Terms of Agreement. In no event will the total paid by the City to the District under this
AGREEMENT exceed the accepted bid amount or 150% of the initial established cost estimates
outlined above ($177,000.00) whichever is less, without modification to this AGREEMENT.

6.
Responsibilities of the District.  The District shall:

A.
Include the construction drawings reviewed and approved by the City for the
Carlson Street improvements in the overall construction drawings for the project.

B.
Supply bidding services for the project construction. The Carlson Street
improvements shall be separated in the bid schedule such that the total construction cost
for any additional the City’s portion of the project is distinct.

C.
Award the project to the successful bidder.

D.
Administer the project, subject to the responsibilities of the City outlined below.

E.
Pay the successful contractor for work properly completed on the project.

F.
Commission and pay for a survey of the 3.3-acre parcel at South High School.

G.
The District shall furnish and perpetually maintain to the satisfaction of the City
the flexible tubular markers located at the site approach on Powderhouse Road.
